@intent The wraith's battle music waits for its spawn animation to finish, then plays while the wraith is within 64 blocks -- it shrugs off /kill by design -- and stops once the player is out of its range
@step arena
gamemode creative
time set day
weather clear
gamerule doDaylightCycle false
gamerule doMobSpawning false
execute if entity @e[type=!minecraft:player] run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]

@step no music during the 110-tick spawn animation
summon the_last_sword:the_last_end_sword_wraith ~ ~ ~8
@wait 3s
# while it is not ready the music handler must stay silent
@assert execute if entity @e[type=the_last_sword:the_last_end_sword_wraith,distance=..16]
@shot spawning

@step music once it is ready
@expect sound the_last_sword:the_last_end_sword_wraith within 10s

@step it shrugs off /kill, and the music plays on
# measured: /kill reports "Killed" but the wraith stays -- its "true health" (TrueHealthManager) is not the vanilla
# health /kill zeroes. That is the mod's design for its bosses, so the script proves it rather than fights it
kill @e[type=the_last_sword:the_last_end_sword_wraith]
@wait 3s
@assert execute if entity @e[type=the_last_sword:the_last_end_sword_wraith]
@assert execute if entity @e[type=the_last_sword:the_last_end_sword_wraith,distance=..16]

@step out of its range, the music stops
# the music handler looks for a ready wraith within 64 blocks of the player, once a second
tp @s ~ ~ ~200
@expect sound the_last_sword:the_last_end_sword_wraith gone within 10s
@shot silence
